Title: Stellar Nursery
Credit: Written by
Author: Peter Colter & Patrick Hale
Contact: patrick@carrioncreek.com

> FADE IN/OUT:

> OVER BLACK:

SUPER: For mothers.

INT. INTERROGATION ROOM - STUDIO

BOOM-BOOM. WHOOSH.

The sound of the inside of a womb. A heartbeat. A memory. BOOM-CLICK.

CUT TO:

CLICK-CLICK.

A pool of light beams down onto a standard flat, nineties, two-cushion couch.

INGRID (30s) lays flat, face up with her arms tucked at her sides. Her hair is damp - matted with dirt and dried pine needles. Her fingernails are split.

Ingrid's breath doesn't echo. The room has a deadening effect — like speaking inside of a sound booth.

INGRID
Lotus!

THERAPIST (O.S.)
(flat, no inflection)
The transition can be disorienting - the effects will dissipate.

Something CLICKS in the darkness. The CLICK is slightly too resonant, metallic, almost biological - more Buck Rogers than BIC.

THERAPIST (O.S.) (CONT'D)
Your vitals show a spike in cortisol -

INGRID
(interrupts)
Where is Lotus?

Ingrid opens her eyes and rubs her split fingernails together, using the pain to ground her.

THERAPIST (O.S.)
You were grieving a child that you hadn't lost yet... Why?

Another CLICK.

THERAPIST (O.S.) (CONT'D)
What is the very first thing you remember?

She breathes shallow, quick breaths. Her eyes dart beneath her eyelids.

INGRID
I was...
(beat)
I had an appointment.

THERAPIST (O.S.)
Location. Coordinates.
(beat)
Where, Ingrid?

Ingrid closes her eyes.

INGRID
I was supposed to give a speech? Or - introduce something... I can't remember honestly.

THERAPIST (O.S.)
Physical sensations & olfactory stimulation produce the best results. What did you touch?

Ingrid's fingers twitch, mimicking a small cylinder of lipstick, triggering her memory.

INGRID
Cherry.
(beat)
The silver tube of my lipstick.

THERAPIST (O.S.)
Good. Hold that. Now what?

INGRID
I see a mirror. I -

CLICK-CLICK.

EXT. PARKING LOT - DAY - CONTINUOUS

CLICK-CLICK.

Ingrid shuts the car door.

The asphalt radiates midday heat.

She pops open her cherry red lipstick and begins applying it while looking at her reflection in the driver's side window.

The muffled HICCUPING LAUGHTER of a baby comes through the glass window.

Ingrid FREEZES and checks the backseat.

THE CRUSHED BABY SEAT. Tempered glass sparkles over a tiny blue blanket.

She slams her hands on the side of the car - trying to rid herself of the intrusive thought.

INGRID
She's -
(beat)
No. No.

She calms herself and clicks the lid shut on the silver tube of lipstick.

CLICK.

INGRID (CONT'D)
It's not real.

Pursing her lips she grabs her portfolio and walks across the lot - the sound of CRUNCHING SAFETY GLASS under her boots on the asphalt makes her wince.

INGRID (CONT'D)
It's not real -

She adjusts her blazer.

INGRID (CONT'D)
Shit.

Ingrid slows and pats down her jacket. Empty.

INGRID (CONT'D)
Don't tell me I...

She unzips the portfolio and looks inside.

INGRID (CONT'D)
Come on, be here - be here.

Empty.

She sprints back toward her car. She yanks the door open, grabs her laminated NASA "PROJECT NURSERY" badge and loops the lanyard around her neck.

THERAPIST (V.O.)
Ingrid -

The sunlight FLICKERS like a giant dying bulb.

INGRID (V.O.)
Something's wrong.

Ingrid looks up at the sky as a deep violet shadow grows across her face.

THERAPIST (V.O.)
Focus.

She shields her eyes.

INGRID (V.O.)
I see - you...

The sky above the parking lot turns a bruised, unnatural violet.

JACK (V.O.)
No -
(shouting)
not here!

Ingrid falls backward.

MATCH CUT TO:

EXT. WOODS - DAY

Ingrid's body hits the forest floor. Her eyes sputter in their sockets as she rolls her body to face the other direction.

Jack's feet nervously tap the ground inches from her face.

She mouths the words "JACK".

ANGRY ALIEN CLICKS. An argument. Ingrid reaches for his foot. She squeezes it.

CLICK-CLICK.

JACK
(to Alien O.S.)
Bathroom - at least until...

Ingrid brings her hand to her face - in it is Jack's NASA "PROJECT NURSERY" badge - she must've ripped it off him in the struggle. She pockets the badge and looks up.

The sky darkens with swarms of Alien craft blotting out the sun. Ingrid's face falls into shadow as the midday heat instantly drops to freezing. She instinctively clutches her arms around herself.

INT. INTERROGATION ROOM - STUDIO

Ingrid sits up on the couch, crossing her arms and shivering. She presses on her split fingernail. It hurts. This is real.

THERAPIST (O.S.)
The past.

She smacks her lips together.

INGRID
Can I get some water?

SILENCE.

THERAPIST (O.S.)
You had a satisfactory amount when you came on board.

An angry, resonant CLICK comes from another area of the room- rebutting the Therapist's poor choice of words.

INGRID
What?

SILENCE.

INGRID (CONT'D)
Just water.

SILENCE.

THERAPIST (O.S.)
We gave you an injection of stimulants and a point nine percent sodium chloride -

INGRID
Give me water!

CLICK-CLICK.

A table pushes up from the ground in front of her with a single glass of water. Ingrid takes the cup and SWIGS it.

THERAPIST (O.S.)
The more we talk, the less time we have to find her.

She searches the dark room with her eyes. She lays back.

THERAPIST (O.S.) (CONT'D)
Your instincts are most important.

INGRID
The next thing I -

Ingrid's eyes roll back.

INGRID (CONT'D)
Cold.
(beat)
My feet were cold.

She shivers, trying to relax.

THERAPIST (O.S.)
What about Jack?

INGRID
How do you know about -

THERAPIST (O.S.)
Relax. Now -

She CHOKES, coughing on invisible water as the timeline shifts.

THERAPIST (O.S.) (CONT'D)
The night itself.

MATCH CUT TO:

INT. BATHROOM - NIGHT

Ingrid COUGHS and SPUTTERS as water enters her mouth. Her eyes bolt open.

The dim yellow tainted lights flicker from a plastic covering that cast a familiar nineties glow in the bathroom.

INGRID
(calling out)
Jack!

She claws the shower curtain around her, shivering. She is in her nightgown. Her hair is matted with pine needles.

INGRID (CONT'D)
Jack?

Silence. She blinks and wipes the wet from her eyes.

INGRID (CONT'D)
Jack, thank god -

Her posture slumps.

INGRID (CONT'D)
Where's the baby?

Heavy FOOTSTEPS approach the hallway side of the door.

JACK (O.S.)
You almost killed her.

INGRID
Jack? Who are you talking to?

Her breath catches in her throat.

JACK (O.S.)
She's the one you want -

A moment of dread spreads across her face.

INGRID
(choked whisper)
Jack?

A THUMP on the door. Feet shuffle.

JACK (O.S.)
(scared)
Hey, hey get off me.

KA-THUNK. The sound of a body hitting a wood floor. She puts a hand over her mouth to steady her quivering head.

INGRID
(choked whisper)
Jack!

She waits and watches for movement at the bottom of the door.

Blood slowly begins to seep into the bathroom. She shakes her head in disbelief, she mouths the word Jack but nothing comes out but her sputtering breath.

Moments pass as she waits in silent disbelief, staring at the door. She shivers then - CLICK. CLICK.

TWO LONG GRAY FINGERS slide under the door.

INGRID (CONT'D)
(panicked)
What?

THUMP! A SLAM on the door. Ingrid SLIPS but steadies herself.

A heavy, 90s satellite field phone vibrates off the counter and hits the floor.

Two shadows pass by the door. They stop, lift an unseen weight, and shuffle away. Ingrid FREEZES. CLICK-CLICK. She grabs the door handle with all of her strength. SCALDING HOT.

INGRID (CONT'D)
FUCK!

She holds her hand and kicks at the door. CLICK-CLICK-MAW! Something pounds on the other side.

BLAM! She stares at the doorway. Silence.

The front door SQUEAKS shut in the background. Ingrid grabs the glowing red phone.

She wraps a towel around the scalding doorknob, rips open the door, and runs.

INGRID (O.S.) (CONT'D)
Lotus!

Ingrid runs back into the bathroom shaking.

INGRID (CONT'D)
That's not hers... that's not hers. That's not - her blood.

She looks at her satellite phone. The analog display flickers with ALIEN GLYPHS then back to normal. The bathroom door handle is half-melted, and black burn marks in the shape of a long strange hand appear on the back of the door. The heat scorched through the wood from the outside. She looks up to realize the shower curtain is burned where someone would pull it back.

She pauses. They put her there. She dials 911 and holds the phone to her ear. CLICK-MAW.

An alien dial-tone. She stumbles past the door, petrified, making sure not to touch it.

INT. LIVING ROOM - CONTINUOUS

A bright light shines through the entryway window.

She picks up the nineties era, beige, corded wall phone. CLICK-MAW. She slams the phone on the receiver.

The clock on the wall reads 4:10am. The hands on the dial are frozen in place. She throws a glance down the hallway towards the nursery where her daughter used to sleep.

She edges against the wall towards the kitchen.

INT. KITCHEN - CONTINUOUS

She stops at the wooden block, her eyes locking onto the heavy steel CLEAVER. She forces her fingers around the handle like grabbing live wire. She rips it free. Her grip turns white-knuckled.

EXT. HOUSE / CARPORT - CONTINUOUS

Ingrid charges off the porch, weapon raised.

Sweeping spotlights spin across the yard. In the distance, the dog BARKS on its broken loop. A blinding searchlight hits her dead-on.

She rips open the driver's side door and dives inside.

INT. CAR - CONTINUOUS

She tosses the cleaver onto the passenger seat — away from where Lotus would sit — and slams the door shut.

Ingrid reaches for the pedals. Nothing. The seat is pushed all the way back. Set for Jack. She glances down: the passenger seat is damp, peppered with pine needles.

INGRID (V.O.)
I thought you were against this?

JACK (V.O.)
They are more like us than we realized -
(beat)
A lot more.

She pauses then jams the key in the ignition.

INGRID
Come on, come on!

Through the glass, two searchlights comb the asphalt toward her.

She twists the key. The engine ROARS to life.

EXT. CAR - CONTINUOUS

Ingrid throws the car into reverse, fighting the distant steering wheel. Tires screech against asphalt.

She blows past the suburban sign. For a split second, the lettering scrambles into ALIEN GLYPHS before snapping back: "WELCOME TO CARRION CREEK."

INT. CAR - CONTINUOUS

Ingrid checks the rear-view mirror. She squints - the single light is focused and bright - like the interrogation room.

She brushes the blindness away and stares out the front window. SQUEAK-CLICK-CLICK. A long, gray hand smears down the outside of the driver's side glass. She slams on the brakes and an alien mass flies past her front windshield and onto the pavement.

She screams and hits the gas. The car jumps and then the engine sputters, chokes and dies. She breathes panicked shallow breaths as she looks out around her car. Nothing but thick woods on either side - the property line of Carrion Creek - confirmed by the green welcome sign mere feet from her rear bumper.

Ingrid glances down at the heavy cleaver.

THERAPIST (V.O.)
And the weapon?

Beside her sit the glowing red satellite phone and the cleaver.

INGRID
What if I found her?

She reaches for the blade, then stops. Her hand trembles.

INGRID (CONT'D)
No - how would I hold her?

She pulls her trembling hands back. She snatches the phone.

EXT. WOODS - NIGHT - CONTINUOUS

She cautiously steps out onto the dirt road.

Her second foot barely touches the dirt when a gray, bloodied hand shoots out from beneath the car. Ingrid screams and makes for the tree-line at a dead sprint. She plunges straight into the safety of the darkness and hides. Behind her, a shadow moves in the tree-line. She FREEZES. CLICK-CLICK-MAW.

A heavy bleating, like the call of a moose. A gray hand reaches out and grabs her arm. She SCREAMS and SWATS at the air. Ingrid stumbles through the thick woods. The satellite phone emits a red, pulsing glow.

INGRID
(choked whisper)
LOTUS!

SILENCE. Then - high above the trees a BEAM OF MULTI-COLORED LIGHT forms a narrow spot around her. Ingrid shields her eyes. A MECHANICAL WHIR breaks the silence.

Ingrid closes her eyes, her hands fall beside her body, and she slumps to the ground, lifeless. Her fingers go slack releasing the phone onto the forest floor. A FLASH OF WHITE.

SILENCE. Strange ALIEN GLYPHS appear on the analog display of her satellite phone as it pulses red on the forest floor. A distant RUMBLE shakes the trees and a bright pulse of fiery orange light illuminates the forest floor.

SMASH TO:

INT. INTERROGATION ROOM - STUDIO

The light above Ingrid flickers RED then WHITE mimicking the pulse of the woods. Ingrid sits panting on the couch, swatting at the empty air as if still fighting the gray hands.

INGRID
And... I dropped the phone.
(sniffs the air)
Oh... fire.

THERAPIST (O.S.)
(interrupting)
Almost -

INGRID
I smell fire.

THERAPIST (V.O.)
Perfect recall.

Tears cut lines through the dirt on her face.

INGRID
But, Jack?

A low, mechanical CLICK vibrates through the room's speakers.

THERAPIST (O.S.)
A necessary ruse.

INGRID
(frantic)
For what?

THERAPIST (O.S.)
Our seed, Ingrid.
(beat)
For you.

She lunges across the beam of light into the dark where the therapist sat.

She grasps the air, frantic to find her tormentor, but the chair is EMPTY. Sitting on the cushion is a screen displaying ALIEN GLYPHS that flash across her face.

CLICK-CLICK-MAW. The sound emanates from the phone. Ingrid gropes around the darkness for the edges of the room. She sniffs the air - the smell of sulfur wafts through the permeable walls and lets the ship breathe. She touches the womblike walls, they bend - made from layers of a Lycra-like fabric.

From behind, a long, gray hand reaches out, attempting to seal her in. She parts the membrane with her split nails, and they give way in layers. The horrible pain grounds her as she screams. This is real. The sound of wet, tearing latex and rushing air fills the space between her panicked breaths.

The rage sends her sailing through the final layer of the membrane. The embryonic alien wall gives way to the forest.

EXT. WOODS - NIGHT

A camouflaged craft hovers three feet above the needle-strewn floor. Silent. Waiting. Guttural CLICKS and a wet, mucus-heavy GURGLING.

Layers of her captor's vessel rupture outward from the hull. Ingrid spills onto the damp forest floor. She scrambles upright and looks back. The torn membrane billows behind her, withered and leaking fluid. A heavy THUD hits the earth behind her.

EXT. ALIEN'S POV - INFRARED OVERLAY - CONTINUOUS

An optical display flickers to life. Trees read as bone-white and the sky - a bruised violet and black.

The lens focuses with a WET, MECHANICAL WHIR — tracking Ingrid's pearlescent silhouette as she bolts into the forest. Ingrid bobs and weaves through the black trees.

Ash falls like dead snow. Behind her: heavy, rhythmic THUDS close the distance. Ingrid breaks into a clearing and skids to a halt at the tree-line. The Carrion Creek sign has been bent. Smoke wafts towards her from the distant fires. Her breath starts and stops in anxious fits - her shoulders drop.

Beyond the tree line: the entire horizon is engulfed in fire.

INGRID
No -

The alien circles her as she freezes and tracks a blinking light on the forest floor. The phone CRACKLES to life.

THERAPIST (V.O.)
Where would you run to, Ingrid?

She picks the phone up.

INGRID
No, no, no!

Ingrid stares into the dark.

INGRID (CONT'D)
Why destroy everything?

THERAPIST (V.O.)
You helped - but, of course, you would not remember, would you?

Ingrid reaches into her pockets and clutches Jack's NASA badge.

INGRID
Jack...

The plastic bites into her palm as she pulls the badge out, it reads: "SWAGGERT | NASA | PROJECT NURSERY | MORPHOLOGY"

THERAPIST (V.O.)
His only condition for your removal was not to watch.

INGRID
You killed —

FIERY ORANGE LIGHT flashes through the canopy.

THERAPIST (V.O.)
(throaty whisper)
Millions, Ingrid.

Ingrid's breath hitches, she wavers but holds fast.

INGRID
Lotus...

Her gaze drops to the charred badge.

THERAPIST (V.O.)
We could not depart in the state she was in. We can incubate... Even extend a life. But —

INGRID
You can't -

She darts her eyes, searching the air for the perfect words.

INGRID (CONT'D)
(amazed)
Manufacture devotion?

A beat of static. CLICK. Ash falls all around her as she steps forward, eyes locking onto the lens.

INGRID (CONT'D)
You can create but only a mother can... Oh, -

CLICK-CLICK-MAW.

INGRID (CONT'D)
That's it...
(relieved)
Isn't it?

The red beacon pulses, then steadies.

THERAPIST (V.O.)
Stay and burn. Or live among the stars.

Ingrid squares her shoulders. She closes her eyes and takes a beat. She exhales, and composes herself. Cold and confident, Ingrid raises her head.

INGRID
I will walk onto your ship. I will raise her in your cage. But -
(beat)
She never leaves my sight.

A burst of sharp, overlapping CLICKS over the receiver.

THERAPIST (V.O.)
Agreed. But it will be a very long ride.

INGRID
Good. And if you ever try to separate us—

CLICK-CLICK. She drops the pulsing field phone into the burning ash at her feet.

INGRID (CONT'D)
Now bring me my daughter.

She wipes the soot from her cheek and smooths her nightgown.

INGRID (CONT'D)
She's due for a feeding.

CLICK-CLICK-MAW! A downdraft tears at the branches, whipping her hair.

Ingrid stands motionless, unflinching. A DEAFENING MECHANICAL DRONE harmonizes with the alien CLICKING. HOLD ON INGRID'S FACE.

> FADE TO BLACK.

BOOM-BOOM-WHOOSH.

The sound of the inside of a womb. A heartbeat. A memory.

> FADE IN/OUT:

> CUE SERIES TITLE:

BOOM-CLICK. SUPER: Carrion Creek: Stellar Nursery

> FADE IN/OUT:

> ROLL CREDITS.

Womb sounds continue. BOOM-BA-BOOM. FIVE SECONDS OF BLACK.

> FADE IN:

SUPER: The National Maternal Mental Health Hotline provides 24/7, free, confidential support before, during, and after pregnancy. Call 1-833-TLC-MAMA or visit mchb.hrsa.gov.

> FADE OUT.
